{
  "id": "canva",
  "name": "Canva",
  "kind": "site",
  "category": "Creative",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "chrome.exe",
      "msedge.exe",
      "firefox.exe",
      "brave.exe",
      "vivaldi.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.google.Chrome",
      "com.microsoft.edgemac",
      "org.mozilla.firefox",
      "com.brave.Browser",
      "com.apple.Safari"
    ],
    "window_title": [
      "Canva"
    ]
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://www.canva.com/help/canva-keyboard-shortcuts/",
    "https://www.canva.com/help/canva-accessibility-features/"
  ],
  "note": "The source page's 'Open More actions menu for a selected element' row renders as 'Shift + 10' on both platform tabs (the leading F of F10 is lost to an icon-font glyph); corrected to Shift+F10 using the corroborating table in Canva's accessibility-features article, added as a second source. Text shortcuts: the macOS tab has no 'Checklist' row at all (Windows: Ctrl+Shift+9) so no mac binding is listed rather than guess one. 'Submit comment' shows 'Command + Enter' under both the macOS and Windows tabs (apparent doc bug); only the Mac chord is listed, Windows is left out rather than guess. Skipped as mouse-dependent: 'Select range' (Click first item + Shift + click last item). Skipped as ambiguous: 'Extend selection: Shift + Arrow keys' (no single direction specified, so no one chord represents it). 'Switch tabs to focus on a design tab from 1-8' is expanded into 8 individual actions since a chord takes exactly one key. The 'Desktop app shortcuts' section documents the separate native Canva desktop app, not the browser version this site profile matches (window_title match only fires inside a browser); included under context 'Desktop app' for completeness per source, but these will not fire through this profile's match. 'Re-open last closed tab' had a literal 'Command + Shift-T' typo on the mac tab, normalized to Cmd+Shift+T. Several actions ('Add empty page' / 'Add page break', 'Quit the whole Canva app' / 'Close window') are documented with identical chords under different vendor labels; both are kept as separate actions since their names differ.",
